    historical_tag: Some("The Battle of the Little Bighorn, fought on June 25, 1876, was the most famous engagement of the Great Sioux War. Lieutenant Colonel George Armstrong Custer and five companies of the 7th Cavalry were annihilated by a combined force of Lakota, Cheyenne, and Arapaho warriors led by Sitting Bull, Crazy Horse, and Gall. The battle was a stunning Native victory, but it galvanized the U.S. government into an overwhelming military response that ultimately crushed the Plains tribes\' resistance."),
